            'Let AB and CD be two equal chords of a circle with centre O. Join OA, OB, OC and OD. Since OA = OC and OB = OD (all are radii) and AB = CD (given), triangles OAB and OCD are congruent (SSS). Therefore angle AOB = angle COD, so equal chords subtend equal angles at the centre.',
          explanation: 'This is a standard circle-geometry proof using the congruency of two triangles formed by joining the centre to the endpoints of each chord.',
